"><circle cx="395" cy="38" r="12" fill="#fff" stroke="#b91c1c" stroke-width="2.2"/><text x="395" y="38.5" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="700" fill="#b91c1c">D</text></g><g class="tg"><line x1="280" y1="232" x2="335" y2="270" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1.5"/><circle cx="280" cy="232" r="3" fill="#334155"/></g><g class="tg"><circle cx="335" cy="270" r="12" fill="#fff" stroke="#b91c1c" stroke-width="2.2"/><text x="335" y="270.5" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="700" fill="#b91c1c">A</text></g><g class="tg"><line x1="330" y1="173" x2="428" y2="175" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1.5"/><circle cx="330" cy="173" r="3" fill="#334155"/></g><g class="tg"><circle cx="428" cy="175" r="12" fill="#fff" stroke="#b91c1c" stroke-width="2.2"/><text x="428" y="175.5" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="700" fill="#b91c1c">F</text></g><g class="tg"><line x1="133" y1="216" x2="62" y2="262" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1.5"/><circle cx="133" cy="216" r="3" fill="#334155"/></g><g class="tg"><circle cx="62" cy="262" r="12" fill="#fff" stroke="#b91c1c" stroke-width="2.2"/><text x="62" y="262.5" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="700" fill="#b91c1c">B</text></g><g class="tg"><line x1="78" y1="69" x2="36" y2="42" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="69" r="3" fill="#334155"/></g><g class="tg"><circle cx="36" cy="42" r="12" fill="#fff" stroke="#b91c1c" stroke-width="2.2"/><text x="36" y="42.5" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="700" fill="#b91c1c">C</text></g></g></svg>', 'The Golgi apparatus receives proteins and lipids from the ER, modifies them (for example by glycosylation), sorts and packages them into vesicles for secretion or delivery. Digestion of worn-out organelles is the job of lysosomes.', 'A');
